Unity USD Toolkit patch to OpenUSD v26.05 (commit 2095fafafd033fa23386d7ec6d58c7cc33974518), applied
after openusd-26.05-windows-draco.patch: no build machine name in the TBB libraries the payload
ships.

Applied by Native~/build_openusd.py to a worktree of the pinned commit, never to the clone itself;
its SHA-256 is pinned in Native~/dependency-sources/macos.tsv and linux.tsv. Every change is marked
"Unity USD Toolkit" in the source.

1. build_usd.py builds TBB 2020 from source on macOS and Linux, and TBB's version banner, compiled
   into libtbb and libtbbmalloc, records the building machine's `hostname -s` as BUILD_HOST. The
   payload ships those libraries, so the name of whoever built it shipped too (a default macOS
   host name carries the owner's full name). build_usd.py now replaces `hostname -s` in
   build/version_info_{macos,linux}.sh with "unknown" before building TBB, the way it already
   patches TBB's Makefile and macos.clang.inc, and fails if the script no longer contains it.
   Windows takes Intel's prebuilt TBB, whose banner names Intel's build machine; this patch does
   not touch it, so the Windows record does not pin it.

diff --git a/build_scripts/build_usd.py b/build_scripts/build_usd.py
index 6d3cb55..425d5ef 100644
--- a/build_scripts/build_usd.py
+++ b/build_scripts/build_usd.py
@@ -1060,6 +1060,16 @@ def InstallTBB(context, force, buildArgs):
     else:
         InstallTBB_Linux(context, force, buildArgs)
 
+# Unity USD Toolkit: TBB 2020's version banner, compiled into every TBB library,
+# names the machine that built it (BUILD_HOST, from `hostname -s`), and the
+# payload ships those libraries. Write a neutral name instead. Fails rather than
+# shipping the host name if the script no longer reads it that way.
+def NeutralizeTBBBuildHost(script):
+    if "`hostname -s`" not in open(script, 'r').read():
+        raise RuntimeError("{} no longer runs `hostname -s`; the TBB "
+                           "build host can't be hidden".format(script))
+    PatchFile(script, [("`hostname -s`", "unknown")])
+
 def InstallTBB_Windows(context, force, buildArgs):
     with CurrentWorkingDirectory(DownloadURL(TBB_URL, context, force, 
         TBB_ROOT_DIR_NAME)):
@@ -1077,6 +1087,8 @@ def InstallTBB_Windows(context, force, buildArgs):
 
 def InstallTBB_MacOS(context, force, buildArgs):
     with CurrentWorkingDirectory(DownloadURL(TBB_URL, context, force)):
+        NeutralizeTBBBuildHost("build/version_info_macos.sh")
+
         # Ensure that the tbb build system picks the proper architecture.
         PatchFile("build/macos.clang.inc",
                 [("-m64",
@@ -1191,6 +1203,8 @@ def InstallTBB_MacOS(context, force, buildArgs):
 
 def InstallTBB_Linux(context, force, buildArgs):
     with CurrentWorkingDirectory(DownloadURL(TBB_URL, context, force)):
+        NeutralizeTBBBuildHost("build/version_info_linux.sh")
+
         # Append extra argument controlling libstdc++ ABI if specified.
         AppendCXX11ABIArg("CXXFLAGS", context, buildArgs)
 
